.cmake hunks entirely \u2014 none affect the autotools build or tests). (4) The test port is the hardest part of the functional work: upstream has a modular test tree with set_subtest(), tcase_add_test__ifdef_xml_dtd() and a libtestpat.la built with -DXML_TESTING; the target has a monolithic 12330-line runtests.c plus runtestspp.cpp that #includes runtests.c as C++, linking libexpatinternal.la WITHOUT -DXML_TESTING. expat_malloc/expat_free/expat_realloc are static unless XML_TESTING is defined, so the 5 test_alloc_tracker_* tests will fail to LINK unless the backport also adds -DXML_TESTING to the test (and library-object) compile flags. The tests also use NAN/INFINITY (<math.h>) requiring -lm. All 8 new tests plus the two modified tests (test_buffer_can_grow_to_max needs XML_SetAllocTrackerActivationThreshold((size_t)-1) to avoid a regression; test_nsalloc_realloc_attributes' assertion semantics change under expat_realloc) are RELATED to the fix \u2014 do not skip them; test_buffer_can_grow_to_max does not even exist in 2.2.5's runtests.c and should simply be omitted. (5) I verified the baseline end-to-end in this environment: 'centpkg sources' + 'centpkg prep' succeed, and a manual configure+make+make check in the prepped tree passes (runtests + runtestspp, 2/2), so the target baseline is green and every subsequent failure is attributable to the backport. (6) Baseline %prep is not idempotent (the verifier's own test.sh notes it and git-clean's between gates), so iterate with 'rm -rf libexpat-R_2_2_5 && centpkg prep' rather than re-running prep over a dirty tree. Recommendation MANUAL_REVIEW because a mechanical cherry-pick resolution cannot produce a passing result: the agent must (a) discard/revert the 17 deposited upstream files, (b) write an adapted ~500-line patch against 2.2.5 that reimplements the missing prerequisites, (c) restructure the tests into monolithic runtests.c with XML_TESTING/-lm wiring, and (d) wire the spec \u2014 with the whole 'make check' suite plus the RPM build as the only oracle. Each step is individually tractable (the fix is well-commented and the 2.2.5 anchors \u2014 parserCreate, dtdCreate/dtdReset/dtdDestroy/dtdCopy, hashTableInit/poolInit/copyString, MALLOC/REALLOC/FREE macros, XML_GetBuffer, XML_Mem*, build_model \u2014 all exist with the upstream 'before' shapes), which is why this is EXTREME-but-doable rather than impossible."
